# Needs the display build: flutter build apk --debug --dart-define=PROBE_AGENT=true --dart-define=PROBE_FIXTURE_WIDGETS=display (see the README).
# What each test shows is also in docs/compat/MATRIX.md: a matrix cell is set only from a test that ran.
# A text selector matches a widget's whole text or any part of it, exactly: case and spaces count (see the negative variants).

before each test
  restart the app
  # the last widget of the screen: right after a restart the agent can answer while the screen is still being built (issue #793)
  wait until "Painted rich text" appears

test "a plain Text is seen by its whole text, a part of it, and contains"
  see "Order total: 42.00"
  see "42.00"
  see "Order total" contains "42.00"

test "the spans of a Text.rich are matched as one text, and each span as a part of it"
  see "Hello world"
  see "Hello"
  see "world"

test "the spans of a RichText are matched as one text, and each span as a part of it"
  see "Painted rich text"
  see "rich text"

# What a user sees is cut ("Shipping address: 1600 Amphitheatre…"), but the selector matches the widget's whole string, the cut part included:
# `see` checks the text the app gave the widget, not what was painted.
test "a Text cut with an ellipsis is matched by its whole string, the part that is not painted included"
  see "Shipping address: 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, California, United States of America"
  see "United States of America"

test "every text widget is found by its id"
  see #wf_text
  see #wf_ellipsis
  see #wf_rich
  see #wf_richtext
